# EMDR — session mode names

Internal ids stay `guided` | `free`. User-facing names do not.

## Canonical labels

| Internal | Write (full) | Short |
|---|---|---|
| `guided` | **AI agent-guided session** | **AI agent-guided** |
| `free` | **Self-guided session** | **Self-guided** |

Constants: `SESSION_MODE_*` in `lib/brand.ts`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
"Agent-guided session"
"Free session"
"Free mode"
"Choose Guided or Free"

// ✅ GOOD
"AI agent-guided session"
"Self-guided session"
"Choose AI agent-guided or Self-guided"
```

## Why not “Free session”

**Free** reads as **unpaid / $0**, not “no agent.” The self-run mode is on paid plans too. Never use **Free session**, **Free mode**, or **Free sessions** as the mode name.

OK to keep **free** only for real price: “Start for free”, “7 days free”, “ad-free”, “won’t be charged.”

Trial minutes on that mode: **self-guided set time** — not “Free session time.”

## AI agent-guided (not Agent-guided)

Always **AI agent-guided** for the agent mode. Do not drop “AI.”

Product headlines may still say **AI-guided EMDR**. Wordmark stays **Nura** (never “Nura AI”).

## Admin / code

Admin chrome should use the same labels (**Self-guided**, not Free session). Code/CSS (`freeSessionChromeId`, `mode-free.mp4`, `threads.mode = 'free'`) may stay. Extend `rewriteRetiredBrandCopy` for leftover help text.
